WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.334
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome, welcome, welcome.

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:05.200
Enjoy yourself.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.100
Thank you for watching.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.334
Well, guys,
yesterday was the first Sunday

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:14.167
of the football season,
and, yeah, it was good.

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:16.634
You know, after eating
and drinking for 11 hours,

00:00:16.634 --> 00:00:18.133
I think I speak for
all Americans when I say,

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:19.200
forget Labor Day.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.567
This is the Monday
we needed off.

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:22.467
Don't you think?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:24.901
This is Monday -- Wow.

00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:27.901
That's right, yesterday was the
first Sunday of the NFL season.

00:00:27.901 --> 00:00:33.534
Yeah, there were 14 games and
400 commercials for DraftKings.

00:00:33.534 --> 00:00:35.734
Yeah, there were so
many DraftKings commercials,

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:39.567
the guy who got the most
play time was Kevin Hart.

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:41.334
But this was exciting.

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:44.868
History was made last night
as 45-year-Old Tom Brady became

00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:48.267
the oldest starting quarterback
in NFL history.

00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:50.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:56.133
Yeah, at Brady's age,
when he claps to get the snap,

00:00:56.133 --> 00:00:58.534
all the lights
in his house turn off.

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:01.267
You can tell
Brady's getting up there

00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:02.834
'cause he has to put
tiny tennis balls

00:01:02.834 --> 00:01:05.534
at the bottom of each cleat.

00:01:05.534 --> 00:01:06.801
Yeah, at Brady's age,

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:09.367
the only false start he gets now
is when he's peeing.

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:13.400
Look, guys, it was the first
NFL weekend of the year,

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:18.634
and DirecTV's NFL Sunday Ticket
website and app crashed.

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:21.467
Fans were upset, and many
complained that customer service

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:22.667
wasn't helpful either.

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:24.334
Listen to this call.
I think you'll see why.

00:01:40.334 --> 00:01:41.501
[ Dial tone ]

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.767
"Jiggle the dish"?

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:47.267
"Jiggle the dish.

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:48.901
Jiggle the dish."

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:51.834
Meanwhile, in other sports news,
the Cleveland Guardians were

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:53.501
playing the
Minnesota Twins, right?

00:01:53.501 --> 00:01:55.434
And at one point,
the umpire checked the

00:01:55.434 --> 00:01:57.400
Guardians' pitcher
for a banned substance

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:59.834
known as "sticky stuff."

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:01.234
Sticky stuff.

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:02.300
And his search
was pretty thorough.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.634
This is real.
Take a look at this.

00:02:03.634 --> 00:02:05.567
-Well, it's one of those things
where you have a guy

00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:08.667
that goes to the hair so much.

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:12.868
-What?!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.868 --> 00:02:14.734
That's a bit much.
-Wow.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.968
And who says baseball
can't compete with football?

00:02:16.968 --> 00:02:19.234
You know what I'm saying?
With that...

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:20.734
The umpire looked like
he was a judge at

00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:23.033
the Westminster Dog Show.

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:24.467
Did you guys see this?

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:27.067
Today, President Biden was
in Boston delivering remarks on

00:02:27.067 --> 00:02:28.601
the infrastructure law,

00:02:28.601 --> 00:02:30.501
and then he started talking
about airports

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:31.634
and he got pretty fired up.

00:02:31.634 --> 00:02:32.934
Watch this.

00:02:32.934 --> 00:02:37.567
-Today, not a single, solitary
American airport --

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:40.934
not one -- ranks in
the top 25 in the world.

00:02:40.934 --> 00:02:43.467
The United States of America --

00:02:43.467 --> 00:02:49.133
not one airport ranks in
the top 25 in the world.

00:02:49.133 --> 00:02:50.901
What in the hell's
the matter with us?

00:02:52.601 --> 00:02:54.868
-Whoa!

00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:56.534
-Wow!

00:02:56.534 --> 00:02:59.200
What?

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.767
Wow!

00:03:00.767 --> 00:03:02.400
-That's comin' in hot
for Grandpa Joe.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:03.868
-Yeah, yeah. Right?

00:03:03.868 --> 00:03:04.934
Then they called
his boarding group,

00:03:04.934 --> 00:03:06.067
and Biden was like, "Never mind.

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:08.767
Everything's fine.
Alright, we're all..."

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:10.100
Hey, there's a new book
coming out about

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.834
former President Trump,
and it sounds like

00:03:11.834 --> 00:03:13.300
during his final days in office,

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:14.901
he was thinking about
refusing to leave.

00:03:14.901 --> 00:03:16.300
Listen to this.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:19.567
-Trump repeatedly told aides
following his election loss that

00:03:19.567 --> 00:03:21.367
he would refuse to leave
The White House.

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:25.467
Trump quizzed
nearly everyone around him

00:03:25.467 --> 00:03:26.868
on how to stay in power.

00:03:26.868 --> 00:03:30.234
Among those he reportedly asked,
the valet who bought him

00:03:30.234 --> 00:03:32.701
Diet Coke when Trump
pressed a red button

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:34.200
on his Oval Office desk.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.434 --> 00:03:43.367
-And if all else fails,
Trump was going to keep

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:45.467
kicking his feet so staffers
couldn't put on his shoes.

00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:48.501
He's like, "I'm not leaving.
I'm not leaving."

00:03:48.501 --> 00:03:50.434
Speaking of Trump,
apparently the former president

00:03:50.434 --> 00:03:53.667
wants the government to help pay
for a special master

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:55.634
to review the seized
Mar-a-Lago documents,

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:58.567
but the Justice Department
wants Trump to pay for it.

00:03:58.567 --> 00:04:01.567
Great. Now they have to
agree on a special master

00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:05.133
to decide who has
to pay for the special master.

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:06.968
Well, I saw that,
this weekend, King Charles

00:04:06.968 --> 00:04:08.634
was participating
in a ceremony to mark

00:04:08.634 --> 00:04:11.367
his official rise to the throne,
and there was a moment where

00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:14.334
he got a little testy over some
extra pens on his desk.

00:04:14.334 --> 00:04:15.467
Watch this.

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:23.534
-Noting that the king
is signing "Charles Rex."

00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:25.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:34.367
-Every staffer was like,

00:04:34.367 --> 00:04:36.334
"Well, this is gonna be
a super-fun change.

00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:38.934
Wow."

00:04:38.934 --> 00:04:40.934
Get this -- people on the inside
are saying Charles

00:04:40.934 --> 00:04:43.000
is already dealing with
quite a few problems.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.434
For example, I heard that he
can't decide what to do with

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:48.734
all the palaces left to him
by his mother.

00:04:48.734 --> 00:04:52.267
Kings -- they're just like
the rest of us.

00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:53.934
Apparently, his first order
of business was

00:04:53.934 --> 00:04:57.200
really stretching the definition
of the word "problem."

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.334
It's definitely going to be
weird seeing Charles pop up

00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:01.868
on an episode of
"Love It or List It."

00:05:03.601 --> 00:05:05.934
Meanwhile, I read that all of
Queen Elizabeth's corgis

00:05:05.934 --> 00:05:09.133
are now going to live with
Prince Andrew.

00:05:09.133 --> 00:05:11.133
[ Audience "Awws, laughter ]

00:05:13.834 --> 00:05:15.534
In response,
one of the corgis said...

00:05:22.467 --> 00:05:24.534
And finally, before we go on,
I'd like to take a moment

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:26.634
to thank some of our sponsors
for tonight's show.

00:05:26.634 --> 00:05:28.167
They don't always fit
in the commercial breaks,

00:05:28.167 --> 00:05:30.133
